notes='This page claims a smallest defining pair (E_0,K_0), gives a binomial degree bound, defines CM bimodules, and constructs ψ_Σ by determinant before a base-extension diagram. Check 149.N1: for the d-element subset A of the 2d-element set in the stated permutation action, g Stab(A)↦gA is well defined and bijective onto its orbit: equality of images is exactly membership of g₂⁻¹g₁ in Stab(A). The orbit is contained in the set of d-element subsets, whose cardinality is binom(2d,d). This verifies the combinatorial index bound only. The norm argument is visibly x1_Σ, with a cancelled raised Σ; it was not converted to an exponent to repair the mathematics. Check 149.N2: in the finite split-coordinate description from the stated finiteness hypothesis, 1_Σ has 1 on Σ and 0 on its nonempty CM complement. At x=1 its full-algebra norm is therefore 0, whereas the preceding determinant on t has value 1. Thus the written full-algebra norm formula fails this identity check. Refined formula 149.N3: N(1−1_Σ+x1_Σ) equals the determinant on t, since its diagonal entries are the x-coordinates on Σ and 1 on the complement, giving exactly the same product. This explicit relation explains the alternative exponent reading without changing the ink. Archive number 148.'
record(s,t,r,d,inv,notes,notation=[['Algebra versus ideal',r'\mathfrak A(Σ)=(E⊗K)/\mathfrak U','149','Pointed ornamental A names the quotient; rounded U names the ideal.'],['Norm argument','baseline x1_Σ, raised old Σ cancelled','149','Ink positions decide against silently replacing multiplication by exponentiation.'],['Torus morphism','ψ_Σ','149','Low bowl and descending stem recur in all formulas.']],hand=['The baseline of 1, rather than its tall upper stroke, decides the multiplication in x1_Σ. A crossed older Sigma remains above the live subscript.','The finite-algebra name has a pointed ornamental A; the ideal keeps the rounded U seen on scans 147–148.','The cancelled E before K in the finiteness insertion has three short bars; it is not part of a live tensor product.'],abbreviations=[['réciproqt','réciproquement'],['isom','isomorphisme'],['pts','points'],['ext.','extension']],events=[['149.N1','targeted proof check','The map g Stab(A)↦gA identifies cosets with the orbit of A, contained among the binom(2d,d) subsets of size d.'],['149.N2','refuted, with the refined statement’s id 149.N3','The written N(x1_Σ) gives 0 at x=1 because the complementary split coordinates vanish; the preceding determinant gives 1.'],['149.N3','targeted proof check','N(1−1_Σ+x1_Σ) has x-coordinates on Σ and 1 elsewhere, so its product equals det_t/E(x_t).']],extra='Certainty-only: the algebra name is read as the second alternative, mathfrak A; the crossed f, E and aussi are resolved. No doubt marks remain on this page; medium-confidence choices are identified in the tables.')
